%% Messaging - idempotent delivery and message requests - ADR-009
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor S as Sender
    participant SA as Sender App
    participant API as API - messaging module
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant WS as Socket.IO
    participant RA as Recipient App
    participant W as Worker

    SA->>SA: generate client_message_id (UUIDv7) BEFORE sending
    SA->>SA: show optimistic bubble - state SENDING
    SA->>API: POST /conversations/{id}/messages

    API->>DB: check block either direction (BR-025)
    alt blocked
        API-->>SA: refused - NEVER discloses the block (MSG-FR-006)
    end

    API->>DB: INSERT message ON CONFLICT (conversation_id, client_message_id) DO NOTHING
    Note right of DB: unique constraint makes retry idempotent<br/>EDGE-020, EDGE-021
    API->>DB: PERSIST before acknowledging
    API-->>SA: 201 with server timestamp - bubble becomes SENT

    alt recipient follows sender - accepted conversation
        API->>WS: emit to recipient room
        WS->>RA: new message within 3s (NFR-PERF-007)
        API->>DB: enqueue push notification
        W->>RA: FCM push (NOTIF-FR-004)
    else recipient does NOT follow sender - MESSAGE REQUEST
        API->>DB: conversation state = REQUEST (MSG-FR-005)
        API->>WS: emit request-count update only
        Note right of W: NO PUSH NOTIFICATION EVER<br/>BR-027 - this is the safety property
    end

    Note over RA,DB: RECIPIENT DECIDES - MSG-FR-005
    RA->>API: accept / decline / block
    alt accept
        API->>DB: state = ACCEPTED - moves to inbox
    else decline
        API->>DB: state = DECLINED
        Note right of API: sender receives NO signal (BR-028)
    end

    Note over SA,DB: FALLBACK if realtime unavailable
    SA->>API: GET /conversations/{id}/messages?since=...
    Note right of SA: polling reuses the SAME client_message_id,<br/>so transport switching cannot duplicate
